{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/596230-did-berlin-have-2-princes-during-the-cold-war","id":596230,"title":"Did berlin have 2 princes during the cold war?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-19T16:01:02-07:00","id":596230,"title":"Did berlin have 2 princes during the cold war?","content":"Does it say this anywhere am a bit curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T17:47:23-07:00","id":596345,"title":"","content":"I think it isn't said anywhere. Its up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T18:52:20-07:00","id":596395,"title":"","content":"In first edition, yes. From Damnation City, 'Two Princes, an old Prussian campaigner from the West and a newly minted Carthian zealot in the East, claimed the city; the conflict, fought out in the midst of reunification street parties, ended both of their Requiems and left no one faction in control.'<br /> <br /> In second edition, there may have been more. West Berlin had Joachim Hirsch, East Berlin's history doesn't get too much into detail. 'East Berlin, when the wall fell, had been rent with half a century's unceasing power struggle, and the margrave quickly found allies there who simply wanted peace to return. He annexed the domain into his own in less than a year.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:27:16-07:00","id":596672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/596230-did-berlin-have-2-princes-during-the-cold-war?p=596395#post596395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In first edition, yes. From Damnation City, 'Two Princes, an old Prussian campaigner from the West and a newly minted Carthian zealot in the East, claimed the city; the conflict, fought out in the midst of reunification street parties, ended both of their Requiems and left no one faction in control.'<br /> <br /> In second edition, there may have been more. West Berlin had Joachim Hirsch, East Berlin's history doesn't get too much into detail. 'East Berlin, when the wall fell, had been rent with half a century's unceasing power struggle, and the margrave quickly found allies there who simply wanted peace to return. He annexed the domain into his own in less than a year.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is kind of important to note whenever discussing NWoD stuff that, because the game mostly doesn't have a &quot;canon&quot; in the same way OWoD does, there could eventually be eight different versions of Berlin's vampire courts published that all contradict each other, and it wouldn't really be seen as an issue. All of the different domain examples really are built more like, well, examples instead of a statement about the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T04:44:26-07:00","id":596714,"title":"","content":"As a practical matter, unless vampires have a reliable way between the two halves of the city - underground, one would assume - then two polities are likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:38:51-07:00","id":597491,"title":"","content":"I quite like the idea of kindred having their own way between the halves of the city. It emphasises that the mortal and kindred worlds may intersect or overlap, but they're still different and separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T07:15:53-07:00","id":598320,"title":"","content":"Given a fair few gangrel can <i>fly</i> that shouldn't be difficult to justify at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:28:34-07:00","id":598931,"title":"","content":"Given the time period as well cameras were probably quite unlikely. It's entirely possible to just climb over while obfuscated, right? A bit risky, but an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T23:31:48-07:00","id":599059,"title":"","content":"No need to climb or fly. Just walk obfuscated past the guards at one of the border crossings (e.g. Checkpoint Charlie). Dominate will do the trick, too (&quot;These papers are fine.&quot;), as will a clever use of Majesty.<br /> And citizens of West Berlin had next to no trouble passing to and fro, anyway. Remember, the wall was designed to keep GDR-citizens <i>in</i>, not to keep FRG-citizens out. As kid, I crossed the border myself, several times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","user":"Quinn","date":".  Grammar fix. 07-22-2015, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}